      "latePostId": "69e9de9cc03088bf3dec5f04",
      "content": "The US government will pay you higher interest than most savings accounts — with zero broker fees 💸\n\nTreasuryDirect.gov: What It Is\n\nThe basics:\n→ US Treasury's official direct-purchase platform: treasurydirect.gov\n→ Buy T-bills, T-notes, bonds, I Bonds, TIPS directly from the government\n→ No brokerage account needed\n→ Zero broker fees, zero markup, zero bid-ask spread\n→ Auction price = same as what institutional investors pay\n→ $100 minimum purchase\n\nThe yield advantage (2023-2024):\n→ 26-week T-bill APY: ~5.0-5.5%\n→ National average savings account: <1%\n→ Best high-yield savings accounts: 3.7-4.2%\n→ T-bills paid 1-1.5% more than the best HYSAs\n→ With zero credit risk\n\nThe tax advantage:\n→ Treasury interest exempt from state AND local taxes\n→ High-tax states: NY (up to 10.9%), CA (13.3%), NJ (10.75%)\n→ A 5.3% T-bill in NY effectively beats a 5.3% HYSA by ~1% after state tax\n→ Most people underestimate this advantage\n\nZero default risk:\n→ Backed by the full faith and credit of the US government\n→ The same entity that issues the currency\n→ Categorically safer than a savings account (which is the bank's liability)\n→ The safest USD asset that exists\n\nAuto-reinvestment:\n→ Set T-bills to auto-reinvest at maturity — up to 2 rollovers\n→ 26-week T-bill with rollover = 18 months of compounding, zero action required\n\nFriction:\n→ Dated interface, must link a bank account\n→ Selling early requires transferring to a broker (~2 days)\n→ For money you won't need during the maturity window: entirely worth it\n\nOne URL: treasurydirect.gov\n\n#moneyfacts #treasurydirect #tbills #investing #personalfinance #financialliteracy #savingsaccount #interestrates #taxstrategy #moneytips",
