      "content": "On-time rent payments don't build credit scores by default — zero of it reports automatically. Mortg\n\nOn-time rent payments don't build credit scores by default — zero of it reports automatically. Mortgage payments build credit from day one. A $1,200/month renter pays $14,400/year that leaves no credit trace. Rental reporting services can add 30-50+ FICO points. Fannie Mae now counts positive rent history in mortgage underwriting. #moneyfacts #creditscorethings #rent #creditbuilding #financialliteracy",
