      "latePostId": "69e9dea37eb34a30e6b674cb",
      "content": "You can pay rent perfectly for 10 years and have nothing to show on your credit report 💸\n\nRent + Credit: The Structural Problem\n\nHow the credit system works:\n→ FICO and VantageScore built from credit bureau data\n→ Bureaus receive data from creditors: banks, card companies, mortgage servicers\n→ They receive it because those creditors also USE bureau data — mutual system\n→ Most landlords are NOT credit bureau clients\n→ No reporting agreement = perfect rent payment = zero credit data\n\nThe mortgage comparison:\n→ First mortgage payment: reported to all 3 bureaus immediately\n→ Renter paying $1,200/month perfectly for 10 years: nothing in credit file\n→ $144,000 in on-time payments that leave no credit trace\n\nWhy this matters structurally:\n→ Renters ≠ less financially responsible\n→ Renters skew younger, lower-income, or in expensive urban markets\n→ Thinner credit files → higher borrowing costs when they do borrow\n→ Or disqualification from housing/jobs requiring credit checks\n→ The system captures people who already have formal credit\n\nHow to fix it:\n\nExperian RentBureau:\n→ Landlord reports directly — tenant doesn't need to do anything\n\nRental Kharma / RentReporters:\n→ Tenant-initiated, works WITHOUT landlord cooperation\n→ Verifies via bank statement or bank connection\n→ Can add up to 2 years retroactive history\n→ Reported FICO increases: 30-50+ points\n\nFannie Mae (2022 update):\n→ Desktop Underwriter now considers positive rent payment history\n→ Consistent rent debits from your bank account → can help mortgage qualification\n→ First time rental data formally counted in major mortgage underwriting\n\n#moneyfacts #creditscorethings #rent #creditbuilding #financialliteracy #creditrepair #ficoscore #personalfinance #renting #housing",
